    "chunk_text": "Yes, we were in power when the Easter attacks occurred. Before the constitutional coup which took place, I was the Minister of Law and Order. But at the time of the Easter Attacks took place the Minister of Law and Order was then President Maithripala Sirisena. As per my knowledge and understanding SIS reports are sent to the President and to the Minister of Public Security, the IGP and the Secretary of the Ministry of Law and Order. Other officials of the government were not informed about this.\n\nI will refrain from commenting about the judicial decision. We request the government to find the perpetrators of this crime and\u00a0bring them to court.\n\nQ Do you think that you can now guarantee such an incident would not occur under a future government you intend to set up?\n\nWhen I was the Minister of Law and Order there were reports about a clash between devotees of certain mosques. We also received information about Saharan. Acting on that information we obtained a blue warrant to arrest him.\n\nIn my opinion, the position of Minister of Law and Order should be assigned to a single person who is committed full time to the cause of national security. When the responsible authorities possessed information and failed to take action, that definitely amounts\u00a0to a serious issue.\n\nIn my opinion, the position of Minister of Law and Order should be assigned to a single person who is committed full time to the cause of national security. When the responsible authorities possessed information and failed to take action, that definitely amounts to a serious issue\n\nToday the government has failed to provide security to even the prisoners. There are many shootings happening in different parts of the country. The government should take steps to ensure that there is more national security. I ensure that under a future regime of ours we would ensure the security of the people."
