    "description": "Sri Lanka seeks deeper India market access for gems, jewellery",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/Sri-Lanka-seeks-deeper-India-market-access-for-gems-jewellery/34-795922",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1786580855.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-08-13-dailyftlk-41e84315-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "70fcc2cf53ff2390016274edaa49dee7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1935,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka seeks deeper India market access for gems, jewellery\n\nSri Lanka business delegation meets with Indian chambers, buyers and industry stakeholders to identify sourcing, investment, manufacturing and business partnership opportunities\n\nEDB and NGJA position Sri Lanka\u2019s natural gemstones, skilled craftsmanship and ethical sourcing credentials as key differentiators\n\nInitiative also leveraged to promote FACETS 2027, Gem City Ratnapura, Gem Sri Lanka and upcoming Sri Lanka Expo 2027\n\nSri Lanka is stepping up efforts to deepen its presence in India\u2019s vast gem and jewellery market, with the Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB) leading a business delegation aimed at unlocking new trade, investment and commercial partnerships.\n\nOrganised with the support of the Sri Lanka High Commission in New Delhi and the Sri Lanka Consulate in Mumbai, the delegation is in India from 8 to 13 August, bringing together senior officials, industry associations and leading Sri Lankan gem and jewellery companies.\n\nThe initiative comes as Sri Lanka seeks to diversify and expand its export markets, with India\u2019s position as a major global jewellery manufacturing and trading hub offering significant opportunities for Sri Lankan gemstone suppliers, jewellers and value-added exporters.\n\nThe delegation includes EDB Chairman, the Chairman of the National Gem & Jewellery Authority (NGJA), EDB officials, representatives of the Sri Lanka Gem & Jewellery Association, Lanka Gem Dealers & Miners Association and Ceylon Gem & Jewellery Traders Association, as well as companies including Gem Paradise, Punsiri Gems, Mansoor Gems, Beauty Gems, Gemluxe Ceylon, Ashadi Jewellers, GemTrad, Ceylon Gemora and Cey Gems.\n\nThe first two days of the program focused on the India International Jewellery Show (IIJS) in Mumbai, where the Sri Lankan delegation engaged with leading buyers, exhibitors, industry stakeholders and members of the show."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-08-13-dailyftlk-41e84315",
    "num": "dailyftlk-41e84315",
    "date_str": "2026-08-13",
    "description": "Sri Lanka seeks deeper India market access for gems, jewellery",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/Sri-Lanka-seeks-deeper-India-market-access-for-gems-jewellery/34-795922",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1786580855.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-08-13-dailyftlk-41e84315-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "70ac5b7002a70f2c72e688e962764f1f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1954,
    "chunk_text": "The first two days of the program focused on the India International Jewellery Show (IIJS) in Mumbai, where the Sri Lankan delegation engaged with leading buyers, exhibitors, industry stakeholders and members of the show.\n\nThe program subsequently shifted towards trade and investment promotion, with meetings held on 10 August with the Bombay Chamber of Commerce and Industry (BCCI) and Maharashtra Chambers of Commerce, Industry & Agriculture (MACCIA).\n\nAddressing the gatherings, the Consul General of Sri Lanka in Mumbai Priyanga Wickramasinghe underscored the importance of closer commercial ties and greater interaction between the two countries\u2019 business communities.\n\nEDB Chairman Mangala Wijesinghe outlined trade and investment opportunities, with particular emphasis on expanding cooperation in gems and jewellery through increased sourcing, partnerships, investment and business collaborations.\n\nThe NGJA Chairman Dr. S.P. Chaminda highlighted Sri Lanka\u2019s reputation for natural gemstones and its strengths in craftsmanship and industry expertise, while promoting investment opportunities across the sector.\n\nSri Lankan participating companies also made individual presentations to Indian business representatives, showcasing their products, capabilities and areas of interest. The EDB said these engagements were intended to strengthen awareness of Sri Lanka as a premium source of ethically sourced gemstones, jewellery and value-added products.\n\nIndustry associations also promoted major Sri Lankan industry events, including Gem City Ratnapura, FACETS 2027 and Gem Sri Lanka, as platforms for Indian buyers and investors to deepen their engagement with the local industry.\n\nThe program continued on 11 and 12 August with engagements involving the World Trade Centre Mumbai, All India Association of Industries, International Chamber of Investment and Business (ICIB) and Mahratta Chamber of Commerce, Industries & Agriculture in Pune."
  },
