    "chunk_size_bytes": 1621,
    "chunk_text": "Oceans Talent set to double Sri Lankan workforce as embedded employment model gains traction\n\nUnited States-based talent hub Oceans Talent is gearing up to double its Sri Lankan workforce as it scales a highly integrated alternative to the traditional business process outsourcing sector.\n\nFounded in 2021 by Chief Executive Officer Ian Myers, the remote-first organisation connects local professionals\u2014referred to internally as divers\u2014with global start-ups and fast-growing businesses. Cementing its long-term commitment to the country, Oceans Talent recently launched a physical office at Chitra Lane in Colombo to complement its remote-first structure, giving team members a collaborative space to connect at their own discretion.\n\nUnlike conventional outsourcing frameworks where back-office tasks are shipped offshore to be completed in isolation, Oceans Talent integrates its Sri Lankan talent directly into the core daily operations of its overseas clients. Oceans Chief Experience Officer Matt Wallaert during a recent media roundtable held in Colombo emphasised that the firm is moving away from the traditional BPO blueprint to build deep, authentic workplace relationships.\n\n\u201cThis isn\u2019t traditional BPO, nameless, faceless person. This is a core team member, that you know by name, you see every day, and is firmly embedded,\u201d Wallaert noted. Illustrating this deep integration, Wallaert shared that US founders have previously travelled to Sri Lanka specifically to attend their local team members\u2019 weddings, while other divers have flown to the US to participate in client-wide corporate retreats."
