    "chunk_size_bytes": 1341,
    "chunk_text": "The market demand for this globally integrated employment model has been massive, with Oceans receiving approximately 20,000 applications annually in Sri Lanka.\n\n\u201cEvery year we want to double in size, so hopefully next year we\u2019ll go from 1,000 to 2,000, 2,000 to 4,000,\u201d Wallaert stated.\n\nDespite operating on a remote-first basis, the enthusiasm for physical community was demonstrated during the recent launch of their Colombo office. When an online attendance form was published for the opening day, over 80 professionals signed up within 20 minutes, forcing the team to temporarily take the form down and leading to a friendly waitlist where employees jokingly bid for a spot to attend.\n\nThe company maintains a strong focus on diversity and social responsibility, boasting a 65 percent female workforce participation rate and an average employee age of thirty. Demonstrating its commitment to local communities during challenging times, Oceans previously funded the rebuilding of a flood-damaged school in Galle.\n\nBy focusing on competitive compensation, continuous career progression, and an inclusive work culture, Oceans Talent has reduced its local attrition rate to an industry-low three percent, demonstrating that Sri Lankan professionals can successfully build high-impact global careers without needing to migrate abroad."
