    "chunk_text": "The President also reviewed the Rs. 1 billion programme to establish rural-level rice processing centres, as well as the construction of a potato purchasing centre in Nuwara Eliya and a grain-legume processing centre in Monaragala. He called for new programmes to support big onion and maize farmers.\n\nThe meeting also reviewed programmes of the Food Commissioner\u2019s Department, including the establishment of new warehouse complexes and the installation of solar power systems.\n\nDiscussions focused on strengthening the Co-operative Wholesale Establishment, Lanka Sathosa and the wider co-operative movement to increase competition, improve services and provide consumers with better-quality goods.\n\nThere are approximately 2,100 co-operative outlets across the country, including Co-op Mega City and Co-op City outlets. The President stressed the need to increase their market share while addressing challenges affecting the sector.\n\nIt was also revealed that legislation is being drafted to address management deficiencies identified within the co-operative sector."
