    "md5": "03f1785f7e9b441383e7e57d4f084385",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1798,
    "chunk_text": "Pakistan High Commission celebrates 79th Independence Day in Colombo\n\nPakistan High Commissioner to Sri Lanka Major General (Retd.) Dr. Nayyar Naseer, , HI (M)\n\nThe High Commission of the Islamic Republic of Pakistan and the Pakistani community in Sri Lanka yesterday commemorated Pakistan\u2019s 79th Independence Day, reaffirming the country\u2019s commitment to building a progressive, democratic and prosperous Islamic welfare state.\n\nThe ceremony at the Pakistan High Commission commenced with the hoisting of the national flag by Pakistan High Commissioner to Sri Lanka Major General (Retd.) Dr. Nayyar Naseer, HI (M), accompanied by the national anthem. Special messages from the President and Prime Minister of Pakistan were also read at the event.\n\nIn his keynote address, Dr. Naseer paid tribute to Father of the Nation Quaid-i-Azam Muhammad Ali Jinnah and Thinker of Pakistan Allama Muhammad Iqbal, while reflecting on eight decades of Pakistan\u2019s resilience, faith and progress across the economy, sports, defence and information technology.\n\nReaffirming Pakistan\u2019s resolve to defend its national sovereignty and vital water resources, the High Commissioner said Pakistan remained committed to peaceful coexistence and resolving regional issues, including the Jammu and Kashmir dispute, through dialogue and diplomacy.\n\nTurning to Sri Lanka-Pakistan relations, Dr. Naseer expressed gratitude to the Government and people of Sri Lanka for their longstanding warmth towards Pakistan and highlighted recent institutional progress under the Sri Lanka-Pakistan Free Trade Agreement (FTA).\n\nHe pointed to growing bilateral momentum through industrial and SME linkages between Sri Lankan businesses and hubs in Punjab and Karachi, as well as technology exchanges in the gems and jewellery sector."
  },
